# Data files are generated or downloaded, live in object storage, and are
# never committed. The metadata under catalog/ IS committed; only the bytes it
# describes are not. Git keeps every version of a binary forever, so one large
# file committed once is paid for by every clone from then on.
*.parquet
*.pmtiles
*.tif
*.tiff
*.zarr/
*.copc.laz
*.laz
*.geojsonl
*.gpkg
*.shp
*.zip

# Staged data (uploaded by tools/upload_data.py) and build scratch.
staging-data/
.cache/

# Pipeline scratch on rails: sbatch logs, spools, temp dirs.
pipeline/*.out
pipeline/tmp-*/
pipeline/staged/
pipeline/manifest.txt
# rashid_check.sbatch drops its JSON report and /usr/bin/time log beside the
# job log. They are run artefacts, one per job id, not catalog metadata.
pipeline/rashid-check-*.json
pipeline/rashid-check-*.time
*.out

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# OS, editor, and tooling noise
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.ruff_cache/
.superpowers/

# NFS silly-rename leftovers (a deleted file still held open)
.nfs*

# The raster item tree is generated, not authored: 67,197 item JSONs plus the
# 3,690 zone/GZD catalogs that group them, ~78k files. They are rebuilt by
# `tools/build_raster_items.py items` and published straight from the working
# tree, because tools/publish.py walks the filesystem rather than the index.
# Keeping them out of git costs one generator run and saves every clone from
# carrying a tree that no human edits. The year collections, their README,
# AGENTS and thumbnails stay committed.
catalog/raster/*/zone=*/
